powerpagecomponent.content:
{
  "description": "Switches on the \"Run checks\" button that lets a checker pick a queued case up (AD-076). Turned ON 2026-09-03, once ClaimCasePlugin was registered in DEV. It was held OFF until then because without the plug-in the Web API create still succeeds — the columns it stamps are only business required and Dataverse does not enforce that through the API — so the page would have reported success while the case stayed in the queue and left assignment rows that AD-037 forbids deleting. The queue list itself renders either way. Turning this on in a NEW environment requires the same two prerequisites in this order: the plug-in step registered, then the \"Case Assignment - claim from the queue\" permission uploaded.",
  "value": "true"
}
